EarthMapCreatorO
================
Generate a real-Earth map for Vintage Story.

What you need
-------------
- Vintage Story 1.22.7 and the matching `earthmapcreatoro_<version>.zip` mod.
- To make your own map: `earthmapcreatoro_geo_<version>.zip`, Python 3 and pip.
  Install the mod on both the server and every connecting client. In single-player,
  install it in your usual Vintage Story Mods folder.

Generate a map
--------------
1. Extract the Geo ZIP. From the extracted `Geo/` directory, install the Python
   dependencies:

       python -m pip install -r requirements.txt

   On Linux, use `python3` instead of `python` if needed.

2. Place these inputs in `Geo/datasets/` (create the directory if needed):
   - `ds75_grd.zip` — [GMTED elevation](https://edcintl.cr.usgs.gov/downloads/sciweb1/shared/topo/downloads/GMTED/Grid_ZipFiles/ds75_grd.zip).
   - `gebco_2025_sub_ice_topo.zip` — [GEBCO bathymetry](https://www.gebco.net/data_and_products/gridded_bathymetry_data/). An extracted GEBCO `.nc` file in `Geo/datasets/` also works.
   - `ne_10m_lakes.zip` — [Natural Earth lakes](https://www.naturalearthdata.com/downloads/10m-physical-vectors/).
   - `HydroRIVERS_v10_na_shp/` — extract the [North/Central America HydroRIVERS shapefile](https://www.hydrosheds.org/products/hydrorivers) here; keep its `.shp`, `.shx`, `.dbf`, and `.prj` files together.

   Other required data downloads automatically on the first run. Allow substantial
   free disk space and time; the climate download alone is about 11 GB.

3. Edit `Geo/config.py` for your desired latitude/longitude bounds and
   `FINAL_WIDTH`/`FINAL_LENGTH`. Choose dimensions in multiples of 512 blocks,
   and create a Vintage Story world with the same width and length. The default
   configuration targets a 25,600 × 25,600-block world in western/central North America.

4. From the `Geo/` directory, run:

       python launch.py

   Wait for `=== Pipeline complete ===`. The files to install are
   `Geo/work/build/earthmap.regions` and `Geo/work/build/earthclimate.bin`.
   The PNGs in that directory are for previewing your map.

Play the map
------------
1. Close the game or server before replacing an existing map. Copy **both**
   generated files to the server's Vintage Story data directory:

       Windows: %APPDATA%\VintagestoryData\EarthMap\
       Linux:   ~/.config/VintagestoryData/EarthMap/

   In single-player, your game is the server. Multiplayer clients need the mod,
   but do not need copies of these map files.

2. Install `earthmapcreatoro_<version>.zip` in the Vintage Story Mods folder,
   then start a new world with the dimensions you selected in `Geo/config.py`.
   Keep the world within the generated map area; outside it, terrain is not
   generated. If you change the map later, previously generated chunks do not
   update automatically—use a new world or regenerate those chunks.

3. In game, `/earthmap pos` shows local terrain information, and
   `/earthmap climate` shows local climate information. These commands require
   the server-control privilege.
